Credits

No third-party code is included. The driver uses DoorBird's official LAN API
(LAN-2-LAN API for DoorBird and BirdGuard, revision 0.36,
https://www.doorbird.com/downloads/api_lan.pdf), as Bird Home Automation's
license for that API allows for integrations. How events are registered
(an HTTP favorite per event, attached to the DoorBird's schedule) follows
Home Assistant's DoorBird integration (https://github.com/home-assistant/core,
Apache License 2.0) and the DoorBirdPy library
(https://github.com/klikini/doorbirdpy, MIT License); no code was copied from them.

Control4 interfaces follow the public Snap One DriverWorks documentation
(https://snap-one.github.io/docs-driverworks-fundamentals/).

The test fixtures in tests/ follow the shape of the DoorBird's answers and
describe a made-up home; names, addresses, users and ids in them are invented.
